{
  "rationale": "The plant automata separate sensing and motion: G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles, G2 models its motion commands. The specifications E1-E4 bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative recovery, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors. Recovery from obstacles is directed and minimal, with rapid return to exploration. Only one controllable is enabled per state, and all uncontrollable events are handled in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plant automata for modularity.",
    "Specifications bind perception to safe actions, enforce one-shot recoveries, and maximize exploration progress while guaranteeing safety."
  ],
